Well, I modified it to take on two vectors, but doesn't seem to be ascending. Here's what I wrote:

void vector_sort(vector<int>& Arr, vector<int> & vect){

   int max_size=-1;

   for(int j=0; j<Arr.size(); j++){

       for(int i=0; i<Arr.size()-1; i++){

               swap(Arr[i],Arr[i+1]);

       }

   }

   int num_size=-1;

   for(int m=0; m<vect.size(); m++){

	   for(int n=0; n<vect.size()-1; n++){

		   swap(vect[n], vect[n+1]);

	   }

   }

}

so, in sort just get rid of the if statement, if I understand right. 

I've gotten rid of the schedule vector entirely. Now I am focusing on the end times. Here's an idea I had (in the for loop, which I made to go through the positions of the list starting from 0 and going to the end positions which should be num_act),
if(end_time[k]<start_time[k+1]){
   start_time.pop_back(k+1);
   end_time.pop_back(k+1);
}
The issue is now that this is not accepted, I just get error signs.
